claim.claim-text:
receive an input from the sensor (265), indicating a presence of the obstacle proximate to the sensor (265);
identify the antenna module proximate to the sensor (265) based on accessing a table in which a sensor index of the sensor is related to an antenna module index of the antenna module proximate to the sensor; and
deactivate at least a portion of the identified antenna module based on the input from the sensor and the sensor index.

identify, based on the input from the sensor (265) and a position of the sensor (265) relative to the antenna module, a position of the obstacle relative to the antenna module;
identify beam patterns for beams of the antenna module by accessing the table in which the sensor index of the sensor is related to beam indices of the beams of the antenna module;
determine, based on the beam patterns and the position of the obstacle relative to the antenna module, one or more of the beams that are obstructed by the obstacle; and
deactivate use of the one or more beams that are determined to be obstructed by the obstacle.

determine a subset of activated beams to use for wireless communication;
determine, based on an input from the second sensor, an amount and direction of rotation of the UE; and
modify the determined subset of activated beams based on the determined amount and direction of rotation of the UE.

calculate, based on the amount and direction of rotation of the UE, a change in position of the UE;
translate, based on the calculated change in position of the UE, a first direction associated with the determined subset of activated beams into a second direction associated with the change in position of the UE;
identify beams associated with the translated second direction; and
modify the determined subset of activated beams based on the beams identified as associated with the translated second direction.

collect and save an identity of used codewords;
calculate a distribution of the codewords at a given time duration; and
generate the AOA aware codebook based on a variance of the distribution being smaller than an estimated variance threshold.

receiving an input from a sensor (265) indicating a presence of an obstacle proximate to the sensor (265);
identifying an antenna module proximate to the sensor (265) by accessing a table in which a sensor index of the sensor (265) is related to an antenna module index of the antenna module proximate to the sensor (265); and
deactivating at least a portion of the identified antenna module based on the input from the sensor (265) and the sensor index.

identifying, based on the input from the sensor (265) and a position of the sensor (265) relative to the antenna module, a position of the obstacle relative to the antenna module;
identifying beam patterns for beams of the antenna module by accessing the table in which the sensor index of the sensor (265) is related to beam indices of the beams of the antenna module;
determining, based on the beam patterns and the position of the obstacle relative to the antenna module, one or more of the beams that are obstructed by the obstacle; and
deactivating use of the one or more beams that are determined to be obstructed by the obstacle.

detecting, by a second sensor, rotation of the UE;
determining a subset of activated beams to use for wireless communication;
determining, based on an input from the second sensor, an amount and direction of rotation of the UE; and
modifying the determined subset of activated beams based on the determined amount and direction of rotation of the UE.

calculating, based on the amount and direction of rotation of the UE, a change in position of the UE;
translating, based on the calculated change in position of the UE, a first direction associated with the determined subset of activated beams into a second direction associated with the change in position of the UE;
identifying beams associated with the translated second direction; and
modifying the determined subset of activated beams based on the beams identified as associated with the translated second direction.

estimating a reference signal power from a reference signal;
collecting and saving an identity of used codewords; and
generating the AOA aware codebook based on the estimated reference signal power being lower than an estimated reference power threshold and a variance of the distribution being smaller than an estimated variance threshold.
